 {:id :repl-sibling
  :title "the REPL's model: a class of the do used before it is defined, a test's class named as a java.lang class"
  :kind :repl
  :why "a static initializer or a superclass needing a class defined later in the do (SPEC §9.2), a class of another of the test's packages not yet defined (the packages' order by their imports); a class Enum or Package of the test's package clashes with the namespace's import of java.lang's"
  :decided "survey §6.1, JCS8 (b), JC4"
  :match [#"\(a Java form of the enclosing do\) is not defined yet" #"already refers to: class java\.lang\."
          #"ClassNotFoundException: (?!java|javax|sun|jdk|com\.sun)[a-z]\w*\."]}
 {:id :analysis
  :title "the analysis: forms javac accepted that arbace.classes.analyze refuses (boxing and generic conversions, switch on long and constant labels, qualified super, intersection types, pattern bindings' scope)"
  :kind :analysis
  :why "the Java forms' analysis is erased by design and leaves some of javac's decisions open; each is the converter's or the analysis' to make (JCS11 (c))"
  :decided "survey §6.3, JC5"
  :match [#"Cannot convert" #"switch without default" #"switch on a value of type" #"switch label is not a constant"
          #"No static field super in" #"is not a functional interface" #"for-each over a value of type" #"\^:const local"
          #"Unknown class int" #"Unknown type: (\[C|AX\$)" #"Unable to resolve symbol: (s|Inclass7)$" #"Local not available here"
          #"No enclosing instance of type" #"No matching (static )?method \S+ for argument types \[(\"L(t\d{5}|java/lang/Object|java/lang/Comparable|java/lang/String)|\"I\" \"J\"|\]$|\]; candidates: \(\"\(I\)Ljava/nio)"
          #"No matching constructor of (t\d{5}|java\.lang\.RuntimeException|java/util/AbstractList for argument types \[\]$)"
          #"No method access\$" #"Class not found: java\.lang\.Object;" #"throw of a non-Throwable"
          #"No accessible method (length|test1) in java\.lang\.Object"
          #"No matching constructor of enum constant" #"no conversion to symbol" #"^refused j2g: \S+: analysis: $"]}
 {:id :j2g-go
  :title "j2g: Go that does not compile (a local class's captured values missing from its constructor call, a captured variable undefined in a lambda or a nested local class, an any returned as int32, finalize of a class that does not declare it, a member through a null constant)"
  :kind :j2g
  :level :compiled
  :why "j2g's translation of these forms is not Go gc accepts: the survey's §5.4 kinds that JC2 did not fix (the constant negative index, the constant zero divisor and pattern matching's unused temporaries are fixed); each test is taken out of its shard's program. Since JC2b the subclasses of PrintStream and PrintWriter are j2g's refusals (:j2g-leaf), and a static field named as a derived name is marked (JCS43 (a)): what is left is the capture bugs and their kin"
  :decided "JCS42 (b): fixed in JC5 (doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): JCS40-JCS49\", \"As built: JC2b\")"
  :match [#"^refused Go does not compile: "]}
